==Icelandic==
{{wikipedia|lang=is}}

===Etymology===
From the {{etyl|non|is}} {{m|non|skyr}} meaning "thick curdled milk"<ref>J.Fritzner. Ordbog over det gamle norske Sprog. 1862, Christiania. </ref>. Related to from the terms {{m|non|skjör-ost}} in {{w|Funen|Fjón}}, {{w|Denmark}}, "[[''skjør-ost'']]" or "[[''skjør'']]" in {{w|Norwegian}}, meaning [[buttermilk]] or cultured milk, and many similar terms in Swedish dialects. The Latin term {{m|la|[[lac]] [[concresco|concretum]]|thick milk}} is in [[w:Germania (book)|the book Germania]] by [[w:Tacitus|Tacitus]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/scɪːr/|lang=is}}
* {{rhymes|ɪːr|lang=is}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|n|skyrs|-}}

# [[#English|skyr]]; a [[yogurt]]-like product made of [[curdled]] [[milk]], [[curd]]s stored up for food; a thick dairy product unique to Icelandic cuisine that can be traced back to the [[Viking]]s

